<div class="bios">
          <H2 class="storyHead">Bios</H2>
          <div class="listAlpha" ><span>listed alphabetically</span></div>
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgb src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Peter Beik.jpg" alt="Peter Beik's headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Peter"></a><span class="person">Peter Beik</span> (<span class="role">Ludwig</span>) is thrilled to be making his Rose Valley debut! He has been performing with the Savoy Company of Philadelphia since 2022, including a run as Grand Duke Rudolph in their performance at the International Gilbert &amp; Sullivan Festival in Buxton. He's delighted to be back working with Julie and Florrie after four shows with them in college! <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Don%20Cheetham%20a.jpg" alt="Don Cheetham's headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Don"></a><span class="person">Don Cheetham</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) Previous RVCO shows include parts as Gatch in <i>How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying</i>,  Giorgio in <i>The Gondoliers</i>, Dave Miller in <i>State Fair</i>, the Steward in <i>Rodgers and Hammerstein's Cinderella</i>, Andrew McLaren in <i>Brigadoon</i>, and chorus in several other musicals. Other favorite roles include two in <i>Our Town</i> – Editor Webb (Barley Sheaf Players) and Simon Stimson (St. Peter's Players), as well as Paul Sycamore in <i>You Can't Take It With You</i> (Barley Sheaf Players.) <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Mike%20Dutka%20playbill.jpg" alt="Colin Dahms's headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Colin"></a><span class="person">Colin Dahms</span> (<span class="role">Costumier - Ben Hashbaz, Ensemble</span>) is once again delighted to be on stage with Rose Valley Chorus and Orchestra. This is Colin’s 8th show with RVC&amp;O – he’s not really sure why they keep allowing him to come back, but he’ll keep doing it until they come to their senses – serves them right! Colin loves karaoke, playing Rock Band, being IN a rock band, and pepperoni pizza. End of Line. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
          
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/piratesP2024/headshots/Faith.jpg" alt="Faith Donaher's headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Faith"></a><span class="person">Faith Donaher</span> (<span class="role">Olga</span>) s delighted to be returning for her sixth show with RVC&amp;O. She first joined RVC&amp;O in 2022 to play Cousin Hebe in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>. She has also performed in many G&amp;S operettas with the Bucks County Gilbert and Sullivan Society, appearing as Vittoria in <i>The Gondoliers</i> and Isabel in <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i>. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
          
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Mike%20Dutka%20playbill.jpg" alt="Michael Dutka's headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Mike"></a><span class="person">Michael Dutka</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) is delighted to join RVC&amp;O’s chorus in <i>The Grand Duke</i>. Previous chorus experience includes <i>Cav and Pag</i> with Opera Verissimo, <i>Die Fledermaus</i>, <i>Rigoletto</i>, and <i>Aida</i> with the State Opera of NJ, <i>Amahl and the Night Visitors</i>, <i>Faust</i>, <i>Lucia di Lammermoor</i>, and <i>La Boheme</i> with the Delaware Valley Opera Company, and <i>Abduction From The Seraglio</i>, <i>La Cenerentola</i>, and <i>The Secret</i> with the Bronx Opera. With this rarely-performed work, Michael will have sung twelve of the fourteen G&amp;S operettas. He thanks his fellow cast-members, the music and stage directors, and all the folks at RVC&amp;O who make these productions possible. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
          
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Lisa Franks a.jpg" alt="Lisa Franks' headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="LisaF"></a><span class="person">Lisa Franks</span> (<i>Ensemble, RVC&amp;O Board Member</i>) With <i>The Grand Duke</i>, Lisa (usually a Broadway Baby) now has 4 G&amp;S productions on her resume.  Previous RVC&amp;O appearances include Melissa Frake in <i>State Fair</i>, Godmother in <i>Cinderella</i>, Mrs. Fezziwig in <i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i>.  She understudied Charlotte Hay (<i>Moon Over Buffalo, </i>Walnut St. Theatre).  Other community theater roles include Fiona (<i>Brigadoon</i>), Liza Doolittle (<i>My Fair Lady</i>), Sally Smith (<i>Me and My Girl</i>), Sarah Brown (<i>Guys &amp; Dolls</i>), Marion Paroo (<i>The Music Man</i>), Laurey (<i>Oklahoma!</i>), Agnes Cohan (<i>George M!</i>), and Reno Sweeney (<i>Anything Goes</i>).  When not on stage, Lisa can be found teaching French at Villanova University. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Jocelyn%20Hall%20playbill.jpg" alt="Jocelyn Hall's headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Jocelyn"></a><span class="person">Jocelyn Hall</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) is excited to be in her 4<sup>th</sup> RVC&amp;O and 3<sup>rd</sup> Gilbert and Sullivan production. Previously, she has performed in <i>The Pirettes of Penzance</i> with The Ardensingers. Also <i>The Gondoliers</i>, <i>State Fair</i>, and <i>Rodgers and Hammerstein’s Cinderella</i> with Rose Valley Chorus and Orchestra. She performed in <i>Come Together: A Beatles Cabaret</i> and <i>School House Rock, Jr</i> with Spotlight Theater. She is a vocalist for the band The G C’s, a teen band with Breaking the Barrier Music.  When she is not performing, Jocelyn enjoys playing soccer, tennis, the flute, the piano, kayaking, and spending time with her friends. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Jennifer%20Heller%20a.jpg" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Jen"></a><span class="person">Jennifer Heller</span> (<span class="role">Secretary</span>) is delighted to be performing with her beloved RVC&amp;O family again. Ms. Heller has performed with many community theatre organizations throughout the region starting with RVCO in 2002. Regarding this production she shared, &ldquo;It's hard work but truly a joy with such talented and supportive directors, cast, and crew. As always, I hope this show might inspire an audience member to explore a new hobby. It’s a wonderful community and there's something for everyone both onstage and behind the scenes.&rdquo; She would like to thank her husband for his love and support and cats Audrey, Nutkin, and Tiggywinkle for a daily dose of fuzz and joy. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/patience2023/headshots/laura.jpg" alt="Laura Hull's headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Laura"></a><span class="person">Laura Hull</span> (<i>Lisa</i>) is excited to be performing again with RVC&amp;O! Past roles include Tessa in last fall's production of <i>The Gondoliers</i>, Lady Saphir (<i>Patience</i>), Melissa (<i>Princess Ida</i>), Peep Bo (<i>The Mikado</i>), and Mrs. Cratchit (<i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i>). Before RVCO, Laura was a long time ensemble member of the Savoy Company in Philadelphia appearing in many G&amp;S productions (<i>The Pirates of Penzance</i>, <i>Iolanthe</i>, <i>Ruddigore</i>, <i>The Mikado</i>, <i>The Yeoman of the Guard</i>, <i>The Gondoliers</i>, and <i>Trial By Jury</i>). Laura studies voice with Countertenor Gus Mercante of Wilmington, DE and thanks her husband Rob and their three cats for their love and support. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Doug Kurtze.jpg" alt="Roger Kennedy's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Roger"></a><span class="person">Roger Kennedy</span> (<i>Ensemble) Previous G&amp;S performances: Policeman in <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i>, and Carpenter in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i> with Musical Theater Southwest. First production with Rose Valley. I also sing with the Chester County Choral Society. Over 60 years of vocal experiences in Pennsylvania, Ohio, Kentucky, New York and New Mexico. Studied with Robert Page and Robert Grouthers at Temple Univ; and with Tim Wilsonn, NY Met.  <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Doug Kurtze.jpg" alt="Doug Kurtze's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Doug"></a><span class="person">Doug Kurtze</span> (<i>Ensemble) last appeared as Ralph (aka Ruth) in the Ardensingers' production of <i>The Pirettes of Penzance</i>.  With Rose Valley he has played Sir Joseph Porter in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>, Dr. Daly in <i>The Sorcerer</i>, Timidon in <i>Thespis</i>, Giorgio in <i>The Gondoliers</i>, and the Foreman in <i>Trial by Jury</i>.  He has also appeared as  Old Adam in <i>Ruddigore</i> with Thespis, Etc., and with Ardensingers as Sgt. Pincher in <i>The Emerald Isle</i>, Scynthius in <i>Princess Ida</i>, the Herald in <i>The Grand Duke</i>, and the Carpenter's Mate in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>.  Off stage, look for him dancing with the Kingsessing Morris Men. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/cinderella2024/headshots/Paula.jpg" alt="Paula McGeary's headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Paula"></a><span class="person">Paula McGeary</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble, RVCO Board Member</span>) is excited to perform again with RVC&amp;O. This will be her 4<sup>th</sup> RVCO and 3<sup>rd</sup> Gilbert and Sullivan production. After many years away from the stage, she has recently performed in <i>The Pirettes of Penzance</i> with The Ardensingers and <i>The Gondoliers</i>, <i>State Fair</i>, and <i>Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein’s Cinderella</i> with Rose Valley Chorus and Orchestra. She is grateful that she gets to share this experience with her daughter Jocelyn and loves sharing the stage with her. Paula is thankful for the love, support, and encouragement she gets from her family. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/patience2023/headshots/marie.jpg" alt="Marie Maguire's headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Doug"></a><span class="person">Marie Maguire</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) is happy to be in her fifth production with RVC&amp;O. She loves performing with this wonderfully talented cast and production company. Marie has performed in all 13 Gilbert and Sullivan shows as of the Spring of 2024, where she performed in <i>The Grand Duke</i> with the Savoy Company of Philadelphia. She has sung and danced in 39 Gilbert and Sullivan productions with The Savoy Company, the GSSCC, Thespis, and RVCO. Marie has been a student of dance, acting, and voice for many years.  Marie is thankful to her husband, family, and friends for their support of her stage performances. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Florrie%20Marks%20Playbill.jpg" alt="Florrie Marks headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Florrie"></a><span class="person">Florrie Marks</span> (<span class="role">Music Director</span>) is a past recipient of the Best Musical Director award at the International Gilbert and Sullivan Festival and has music directed the entire G&amp;S canon. Other directing credits include Allenberry Playhouse, the G&amp;S Society of Chester County, Penn Singers, Ardensingers, Ridgewood (NJ) Gilbert &amp; Sullivan Opera Company, Ridgewood High School Alumni Band, and Glen Rock (NJ) Pops Orchestra. For several years, she was also the Music Director of the fall and spring musicals at Archbishop Wood High School. In addition to her conducting activities, she is Director of Music Ministries at Temple Lutheran Church in Havertown. Before picking up the baton on a regular basis, Florrie was a professional violinist, with credits ranging from symphony orchestras to a bluegrass band. She has music directed several of our productions since 2017, most recently last season’s <i>The Gondoliers</i> and <i>How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying</i>, and she is delighted to return this fall to direct this all-too-seldom performed gem of a comic opera! <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="headshots/Julie May.jpg" alt="Julie May's headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Julie"></a><span class="person">Julie May</span> (<span class="role">Stage Director</span>) is pleased to direct RVCO’s <i>The Grand Duke</i> collaborating with Florrie Marks, a long time G&amp;S directorial partner.  Julie previously appeared at RVC&amp;O as Vera Charles in <i>Mame</i> and most recently as Buttercup in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>.    She’s directed 25+ G&amp;S productions, the majority with G&amp;S Society of Chester County as well as Bucks County G&amp;S, Ardensingers, Penn Singers and more in the Delaware Valley, and in England (The Philadelphia Union at the International G&amp;S Festival). She has performed in all 14 G&amp;S operettas with the above, and Savoynet, and in B’way shows at Forge, Theatre, Footlighters, the Barn/The Dramateurs, Swarthmore Player’s Club, Barley Sheaf, winning performance awards in England with Savoynet and at Forge Theatre.  Love to Richard!  Eloia! Eloia! Eloia! to the cast and crew of RVCO’s <i>The Grand Duke</i>! Thank you! <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>     
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Albert Melli a.jpg" alt="Albert Melli's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Albert"></a><span class="person">Albert Melli</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) was last seen with RVC&amp;O in the Spring 2026 production of How To <i>Succeed In Bussiness Without Really Trying</i>. Before that he appeared in the Fall 2025 production of <i>The Gondoliers</i> after a hiatus of nearly 25 years. His RVC&amp;O career began with <i>Trial By Jury</i> in Fall 1982 and ran through Fall 2001 when he was Leonard Meryll in the <i>The Yeomen of the Guard</i>. During that time he also worked with several other groups including the Ardensingers and the late lamented Thespis Etc. Some of the roles he played with these groups included Richard Dauntless, Nanki-Pooh, and Marco. He currently spends his retirement hiking, singing, reading, traveling, and in various other forms of dissipation.  <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Bob%20Moore a.jpg" alt="Robert Moore headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Robert"></a><span class="person">Robert Moore</span> (<span class="role">(Viscount Mentone, Chair of Show Selection Committee, Make-Up Designer</span>) is a Life Member of RVC&amp;O and holds an MA in Theatre from Villanova Univ. He has a long list of professional credits in film, theater, and touring companies and was last seen in <i>How to Succedd in Bussiness Without Really Trying</i>. He also performed in <i>Brigadoon</i> at Longwood Gardens last summer (Brandywiners) and sings in The Brandywiners Chorale. He serves on the artistic staff of the Next Generation Youth Theater where he teaches acting and directs shows. He dedicates this show to the memory of his parents and Bonnie Decktor.  He hopes that you enjoy <i>The Grand Duke</i>! <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/piratesP2024/headshots/Ray.jpg" alt="Ray Murhpy headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Ray"></a><span class="person">Ray Murphy</span> (<span class="role">Herald, Ensemble</span>) has worn many hats as a life member of RVC&amp;O, from playing in the pit, to tackling sets with the tech crew, lingering on the lighting cues, handling the house, practicing patience with the parking lot, and course, chewing the scenery whilst onstage. His most recent role was that of the Duke of Plaza-Toro in <i>The Gondoliers</i>.  Other onstage appearances include the Pirate King in <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i>, Ko-Ko in <i>The Mikado</i>, Zeus in <i>Thespis</i>, Colonel Caverly in <i>Patience</i>, Sir Joseph Porter KCB in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>, Wilfred Shadbolt in <i>The Yeomen of the Guard</i>, and Professor Harold Hill in <i>The Music Man</i>, in addition to parts in <i>Vintage with a Vengeance</i>, <i>Nailed in Vegas</i>, <i>Radio Days</i>, <i>Iolanthe</i>, <i>Ruddigore</i>, <i>Princess Ida</i>, and <i>Trial by Jury</i>. He turned up at Ardensingers in Sullivan's <i>The Emerald Isle</i>, and also took a turn as Mr. Toad in <i>The Wind in the Willows</i> at Opera Delaware. He is appreciative to his wife Jan who supports his theatrical habit, and gives thanks and praise for his gifts and blessings at New Hope Christian Church in Broomall. 1 Corinthians 10:31 <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Steve%20Naz%20a.jpg" alt="Steve Naz's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Naz"></a><span class="person">Steve Naz</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble, RVCO Board Member</span>) This season begins Steve’s fifth year with RVC&amp;O as he suits up to play a resident of Pfennig Halbpfennig, as well as a chamberlain to the Grand Duke, himself, and a toga-wearing jolly, jolly jinkster in the royal court. Between practices and performances, Steve serves as a board member, with responsibilities that include tending to the RVC&amp;O headquarters building. Steve has played in numerous bands and ensembles from elementary school through Temple University’s marching and concert bands, and has been a member of orchestras in various musicals. Off-stage, Steve is a retired I.T. professional and an all-around technologist. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="headshots/Sean O’Donnell.jpg" alt="Sean O’Donnell's headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Sean"></a><span class="person">Sean O’Donnell</span> (<i>Notary - Dr. Tannh&#228;user</i>) is excited to be back on the Rose Valley stage after a 20-year hiatus for <i>The Grand Duke</i>! Since 1999, Sean has performed in 12 of the 14 G&amp;S operettas with The Ardensingers, Rose Valley, and GSSCC. He has also performed with the Opera Delaware Family Workshop, Delaware Humanities Forum, and done solo work including the tenor solo in the Mozart Requiem. Sean has also produced/directed multiple shows including a revival of Sullivan’s last work, <i>The Emerald Isle</i>, in 2025. Sean currently works as a band, chorus, and orchestra teacher in Maryland. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/patience2023/headshots/mary.jpg" alt="Mary Punshon's headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Mary"></a><span class="person">Mary Punshon</span> (<span class="role">Julia Jellicoe</span>) most recently appeared as Lady Angela in <i>Patience</i>.  Her favorite roles with RVC&amp;O roles include Josephine in <i>H.M.S Pinafore</i>, the title role in <i>Iolanthe</i>, Lalume in <i>Kismet</i>, Mad Margaret in <i>Ruddigore</i>, and Phoebe in <i>The Yeomen of the Guard</i>. Mary also represented RVC7am\O at the Gettysburg International G&amp;S Festival as Amanda in <i>The Carp</i>.   Mary was a frequent performer with The Concert Operetta Theater. Among her roles with them were Masha in <i>The Chocolate Soldier</i> at The Music Pier in Ocean City, NJ with The Ocean City Pops and Princess Margaret in <i>The Student Prince</i> at the Academy of Vocal Arts.    <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Caroline Pashos A.jpg" alt="Caroline Pashos's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Caroline"></a><span class="person">Caroline Pashos</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) is excited to return to the stage with RVCO for her seccond season after performing in <i>The Gondoliers</i> and <i>How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying</i> last year. She also performs with the Delaware Valley Opera Company, where she serves on the Board of Directors and as the Chorus Manager. Her credits with them include 14 operas from <i>Carmen</i> to <i>The Merry Widow</i> to <i>Le nozze di Figaro</i>, as well as singing the role of Sister Martha in <i>Dialogues of the Carmelites</i>. She also sings in the choir of Trinity Evangelical Lutheran Church in Lansdale, PA. In 2017, she graduated in from Temple University with a BA in Theatre. Outside of theatre, she loves aviation, nature, roller coasters, and sports. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Chris Rubino a.jpg" alt="Chris Rubino's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Chris"></a><span class="person">Chris Rubino</span> (<span class="role">Ernest, Producer, Set Designer, RVCO President</span>) is proud to be part of this premier for RVC&amp;O, the last of 14 operettas to complete the G&amp;S canon! Memorable RVCO roles include Tolloller in <i>Iolanthe</i>, Dexter in <i>High Society</i>, Marco in <i>The Gondoliers</i>, and Finch in <i>How To Succeed In Business Without Really Trying</i>. Notable set designs include <i>The Sorcerer</i> (2018), <i>A Christmas Carol - the Musical</i> (2019), and <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i> (2024). &ldquo;Much love to my wife Meagan and our two sons Marc and Brian for matching wits with my thespian side. To paraphrase Ernest, a man who can rule a theatrical company can rule anything!&rdquo;  <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/gondoliers2025/headshots/Kathy Sarlsaon.jpg" alt="Kathy Sarlson's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="KathyS"></a><span class="person">Kathy Sarlson</span> (<span class="role">Elsa</span>) is delighted to return to RVCO after playing Giulia in <i>The Gondoliers</i> last fall. Recent credits include <i>Godspell</i> (By My Side soloist) and <i>Kinky Boots</i> (Trish) with Viviana Theatre. Kathy works as a national nonprofit fundraising consultant. With thanks to Julie, Florrie, and the cast and crew for a joyous experience; gratitude to her voice teacher, Christie; and with love always to Ben, Lily, and Aaron. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><a name="Joyce"></a><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/piratesP2024/headshots/Joyce.jpg" alt="Joyce Severin headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Joyce"></a><span class="person">Joyce Severin</span> (<span class="role">Ensemble</span>) is thrilled to be back performing with Rose Valley Chorus &amp; Orchestra in their production of <i>The Grand Duke</i>. This marks her 5th Gilbert and Sullivan show. Last year, Joyce appeared in <i>The Gondoliers</i> with RVC&amp;O both in the Ensemble, and as Inez. Joyce also performs with the Ardensingers, Havertown Choristers, St. Andrew’s Choir, and the William Penn Community Chorus. When not performing, Joyce is the proud mother of 4, and grandmother of 1. She would like to thank her family for their love and support in all  of her ventures. Enjoy the show!<a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/howTo2026/headshots/Jeff%20Swaford%20%20playbill.jpg" alt="Jeff Swafford headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Jeff"></a><span class="person">Jeff Swafford</span> (<span class="role">The Prince of Monte Carlo, Ensemble, RVCO Board Member</span>) enjoys spending time with his RVC&amp;O family. Recent RVC&amp;O roles include <i>How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying</i> (J.B. Biggley), <i>The Gondoliers</i> (Antonio/Ensemble), <i>State Fair</i> (Abel Frake), <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i> (Samuel), <i>Cinderella</i> (King Maximillian), <i>Patience</i> (The Duke of Dunstable), <i>High Society</i> (Mike Connor), <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i> (Dick Deadeye), <i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i> (Bob Cratchit), <i>Naughty Marietta, Revised 2018</i> and <i>The Mikado</i> (Ensemble), and with other local theaters, and <i>Seussical the Musical</i> (Horton). Jeff enjoys the shore, camping, Italian food, red wine, and hopes to revive his love for the piano. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/patience2023/headshots/sharon.jpg" alt="Sharon Weil-Chalker'a headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Sharon"></a><span class="person">Sharon Weil-Chalker</span> (<span class="role">Bertha</span>) is thrilled to return to her childhood passion, in her sixth RVC&amp;O production, including <i>State Fair</i> (not staged in 2020), <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>, <i>Patience</i>, <i>The Gondoliers</i>, and <i>How to Succeed in Bussiness Without Really Trying</i>. Much gratitude to Florrie, Julie, and this wonderful cast that feels like old friends. Sharon sings baritone with Philadelphia Freedom Chorus (women’s barbershop). She sang with Northwestern University Singers, Swarthmore College Chorus, and Singing Moms. She enjoys tap, salsa, and bachata and paddles dragonboat with Making Waves. Favourite roles: By My Side (<i>Godspell</i>), Sylvia Barrett (<i>Up the Down Staircase</i>), and the never staged Hoopla Barker! She plays flute, some piano, and very little guitar. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><a name="Heidi"></a><span class="headshot_img"><imgg src="../pirates2024/headshots/Heidi.jpg" alt="Heidi Williams' headshot" class="headshot"/></span><span class="person">Heidi Williams</span> (<span class="role">Gretchen</span>) is thrilled to join RVC&amp;O as Gretchen in <i>The Grand Duke</i>. Her love of comedy, poetry, music, dance and costumes are all combined in Gilbert and Sullivan. She is grateful to join this fun-loving, joyful, theatrical troupe. Best wishes and good luck to everyone!. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <!--<p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Grace%20Albert%20playbill.jpg" alt="Allie Beik headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Grace"></a><span class="person">Grace Albert</span> (<span class="role">Props</span>) is excited to be helping out this upbeat and vibrant production. She was recently seen as Eleanor, Jeanne and a Fairtone in last years production of <i>State Fair</i>. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Allie Beik a.jpg" alt="Allie Beik headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Allie"></a><span class="person">Allie Beik</span> (<span class="role">Rosemary</span>) is so excited to make her RVCO debut in this incredibly fun production! Her most recent roles have been with NCT in <i>Into the Woods</i> (Cinderella's Stepmother), <i>A Little Night Music</i> (Mrs. Nordstrom), <i>Joseph and the Amazing Technicolor Dreamcoat</i> (Ensemble), and before that with Brooklyn Theatre Club in <i>My Fair Lady</i> (Eliza Doolittle), <i>Into the Woods</i> (Cinderella), <i>The Mystery of Edwin Drood</i> (Rosa Bud), and <i>Suessical</i> (Jojo). She is so thankful to her husband and family for taking on extra toddler time while she rehearses for this show and for their never-ending support!  <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Andrea Broido a.jpg" alt="Andrea Broido headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Andrea"></a><span class="person">Andrea Broido</span> (<span class="role">Miss Jones</span>) is an accomplished soprano recognized for her work in opera, oratorio and recital.  She has sung with Virginia Opera, Opera Delaware, Opera Ensemble of NY, Berks Grand Opera (Reading, PA), Center Stage Opera and Capital Opera (both in Harrisburg, PA), Delaware Valley Opera Co., Rose Valley Chorus &amp; Orchestra and The Arden Club in such roles include Violetta, Mimi, Pamina, Rosalinda, Nedda, Micaela, Donna Elvira, the Countess and the Governess and Hanna Glawari. She has appeared as featured soloist with the Delaware Symphony Orchestra, the Roanoke Symphony, the Terre Haute Symphony (IN), the Concerto Soloists of Phila., the Reading Symphony, Vox Amadeus, as well as numerous appearances with the Lansdowne Symphony Orchestra and PA Pro Musica.  She holds a B.A. in Music from Hollins University (Roanoke, VA) and maintains a private voice studio in the Philadelphia area. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Lisa Cleek a.jpg" alt="Lisa Cleek headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="LisaC"></a><b>Lisa Cleek</b> (<i>Secretary</i>) Having started at RVCO as a sound assistant, Lisa is now a regular fixture, and happy to be part of <i>How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying</i>. She has recently been involved in <i>The Gondoliers</i>, <i>State Fair</i>, <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i> (a few times) and sings with her church choir. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
               
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Ross Druker a.jpg" alt="Ross Druker headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Ross"></a><b>Ross Druker</b> (<i>Twimble/Womper</i>) is happy to be returning to Rose Valley for his fifth show, having appeared as Nanki-Poo in <i>The Mikado</i>, Richard Dauntless in <i>Ruddigore</i>, Captain Corcoran in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>, and Robert Martin in <i>The Drowsy Chaperone</i>.  Recent roles include James in <i>It's Only A Play</i> and the Stage Manager in <i>Our Town</i> at Old Academy Players, Herbie in <i>Gypsy</i> and Mr. Lindquist in <i>A Little Night Music</i> at Narberth Community Theater, Ned Newley in <i>The Outsider</i> and multiple roles in <i>The Laramie Project:Ten Years Later</i> at Spotlight Theatre, Ernie Cusack in <i>Rumors</i>, Mr. Mayhew in <i>Witness for the Prosecution</i>, and Don John in <i>Much Ado About Nothing</i> at Chestnut Hill Stagecrafters.  He has also performed numerous Gilbert and Sullivan lead roles with the Savoy Company in Philadelphia and England.  Ross sings professionally with the West Jersey Chamber Music Society and has sung with The Philadelphia Chorale behind Andrea Bocelli at the Wells Fargo Center in Philadelphia and Madison Square Garden in NYC. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Chris Fitting a.jpg" alt="Chris Fitting headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="ChrisF"></a><b>Chris Fitting</b> (<i>Director</i>) is thrilled to have had the opportunity to work with Rose Valley Chorus &amp; Orchestra on one of his favorite musicals. A member of Actors' Equity Association, Chris has worked at the Walnut Street Theatre, Media Theatre, Candlelight Theatre, Fulton Theatre, and many more. His years as a professional actor inform his collaborative and actor-centered directing approach. He has also directed numerous entertainment programs for senior-living communities throughout Pennsylvania, New Jersey, and Delaware. He is deeply grateful to the cast, orchestra, and creative team for their commitment and trust throughout the rehearsal process. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/patience2023/headshots/laura.jpg" alt="Laura Hull headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Laura"></a><span class="person">Laura Hull</span> (<i>Secretay</i>) is excited to be performing again with RVCO!  Laura recently played Tessa in last fall's production of <i>The Gondoliers</i>. Past roles include Lady Saphir (<i>Patience</i>), Melissa (<i>Princess Ida</i>), Peep Bo (<i>The Mikado</i>), Player Queen (<i>Hamlet</i>), Mrs. Cratchit (<i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i>), and Fanchon (<i>Naughty Marietta, Revised 2018</i>). Before RVCO, Laura was a long time ensemble member of the Savoy Company in Philadelphia appearing in <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i>, <i>Iolanthe</i>, <i>Ruddigore</i>, <i>The Mikado</i>, <i>Yeoman of the Guard</i>, <i>The Gondoliers</i>, and <i>Trial By Jury</i>. Laura studies voice with Countertenor Gus Mercante of Wilmington, DE and thanks her husband Rob and their three cats for their love and support. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/SharonK.jpeg" alt="Sharon Kotzen headshot" class="headshot" style="-webkit-filter: grayscale(100%); /* Safari 6.0 - 9.0 */ filter: grayscale(100%);"/></span><a name="SharonK"></a><span class="person">Sharon Kotzen</span> (<span class="role">Miss Krumholtz</span>) is delighted to return to RVCO for her 3rd performance with this talented group. Two years ago she played the role of the Stepmother in <i>"Rodgers and Hammerstein's Cinderella</i> and last year she had fun being Mrs. Edwin Metcalf in <i>State Fair</i>. Sharon has also had the good fortune to play many wonderful and diverse leading roles with the Ohev Shalom Players in Wallingford. These include: Adelaide in <i>Guys and Dolls</i>, the Witch in <i>Into the Woods</i>, Mama Rose in <i>Gypsy</i>, Rose in <i>Bye Bye Birdie</i>, Ella Peterson in <i>Bells are Ringing</i>, Amy in <i>Company</i>, Golde in <i>Fiddler on the Roof</i>, Older Belle in <i>Little Me</i>, Berthe in <i>Pippin</i>" Charity Barnum in <i>Barnum</i>, Mrs. Paroo in <i>The Music Man</i>, and most recently the Rabbi and Fruma Sarah in <i>Fiddler on the Roof</i>. Now, as a retired teacher and guidance counselor at Ridley High School, Sharon has more time to travel with her husband Stanley and keep busy with her children and grandchildren as they participate in all of their activities. BUT she always makes time to do what she loves to do &hellip; act, sing, and dance on stage. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Bill%20Michael%20a.jpg" alt="Bill Michael headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Bill"></a><span class="person">Bill Michael</span> (<span class="role">Tackaberry, Producer, Webmaster</span>) was last seen with RVCO as Harry in <i>State Fair</i>. Other roles with RVCO include the Solicitor in <i>Patience</i>, George Kitteridge <i>High Society</i>, Ito in <i>Mame</i>, Beadle / Mr. Hawkins / Scrooge's Father in <i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i>, Slim in <i>Oklahoma!</i>, and Jacob Miller in <i>Plain and Fancy</i>, and Pierre in <i>The Red Mill</i>. He has appeared in many RVCO shows in the past 30 plus years and performed just as many roles behind the scenes. This is Bill's 8<sup>th</sup> show as producer for RVCO. A shout-out to the stage manager, my wife Kathy. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Kathy%20Michael%20playbill.jpg" alt="Kathy Michael headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Kathy"></a><span class="person">Kathy Michael</span> (<span class="role">Stage Manager, RVCO Board Secretary</span>) has been a member of RVCO for many years and has held many positions. This show, she is once again the Stage Manager, making sure all runs smoothly. Previously, she has been a lighting designer, stage manager, and director. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p> 
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Philip%20Milone%20playbill.jpg" alt="Philip Milone headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Phil"></a><span class="person">Philip Milone</span> (<span class="role">Lighting Designer</span>) has over 20-year experience in the theatre industry. He spent 12 summers with Dogwood Dell in Richmond, VA, in various positions. Favorite Dell shows include Spamalot, Matilda, Thoroughly Modern Millie, and Spelling Bee. He was the Production Manager at Dominion Energy Center prior to moving to Delco. He is the Technical Director and Designer for Next Generation Theatre in Wallingford-Swarthmore. When not doing theatre Philip enjoys time with his wife and dogs. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>  
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Caity Moon a.jpg" alt="Caity Moon headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Robert"></a><span class="person">Caity Moon</span> (<span class="role">Choreographer</span>) has been involved in theater with Rose Valley since 2009, beginning as a dancer and ensemble member. Over the years, my passion for performance has grown into choreography, where I've had the opportunity to work on productions such as <i>My Fair Lady</i>, <i>The Gondoliers</i>, <i>Oklahoma!</i>, and <i>Annie Get Your Gun</i>. I'm thrilled to now be choreographing <i>How to Succeed in Business Without Really Trying</i> and to be back doing what I love. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Chris Rubino a.jpg" alt="Chris Rubino headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Chris"></a><span class="person">Chris Rubino</span> (<span class="role">J. Pierrepont Finch, RVCO President</span>) () has been performing with RVCO since 2011. Memorable roles include Freddy in <i>My Fair Lady</i>, Ralph in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>, Dexter in <i>High Society</i>, Wayne in <i>State Fair</i>, and Marco in <i>The Gondoliers</i>. Notable set designs include <i>The Sorcerer</i> (2018), <i>A Christmas Carol - the Musical</i> (2019), <i>A Little Night Music</i> (Narberth Community Theater, 2022), and <i>The Pirates of Penzance</i> (2024). &ldquo;Much love to my wife Meagan and our two sons Marc and Brian for encouraging&hellip; ok, tolerating&hellip; my onstage antics. I'm playing this role by the book!&rdquo;  <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Marc Rubino a.jpg" alt="Marc Rubino headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Marc"></a><span class="person">Marc Rubino</span> (<span class="role">Office Intern</span>) is thrilled to be on stage again with RVCO! Previous credits with RVCO include Hercules in <i>The Sorcerer</i> (2018), Jonathan in <i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i> (2019), Midshipmite in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i> (2022), and Royal Page in <i>Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein's Cinderella</i>. He has been an enthusiastic participant in Upper Darby Summer Stage since 2021. Other stage roles include Lumiere in <i>Beauty and the Beast, Jr.</i> (2025), Uncle Fester in <i>The Addams Family the Musical</i> (2024), and Bertrand in <i>A Little Night Music</i> (2022). When not on stage, Marc can be found playing trumpet on the competition field with the 2025 State- and National-champion Upper Darby High School Marching Royals. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Mike Salmanson a.jpg" alt="SMike Salmanson's headshot" class="headshot lighter"/></span><a name="Mike"></a><span class="person">Mike Salmanson</span> (<i>Toynbee</i>) is thrilled to be in his first RVCO production! Former theatrics include <i>The Music Man</i> (crew); <i>South Pacific</i> (SeaBee); <i>Tommy</i> (ensemble); <i>West Side Story</i> (crew); <i>The Mystery of Edwin Drood</i> (ensemble) and <i>Crazy for You</i> (ensemble).  He created, and co-wrote the book, music and lyrics for the award-winning <i>A House Divided</i>, which he directed in its world premiere at Narberth Community Theater.   Along with castmates Lisa Franks and Kate Phillips-Kaiser, he co-founded the Castaways, a small ensemble that performs at various events, including most notably the Narberth Dickens Festival.  When not performing, he is a lawyer and a member of Narberth Borough Council. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Jeff Swaford  playbill.jpg" alt="Jeff Swafford headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Jeff"></a><span class="person">Jeff Swafford</span> (<span class="role">J. B. Biggley, RVCO Board Member</span>) enjoys spending time with his RVCO family. Recent RVCO roles include <i>The Gondoliers</i> (Antonio/Ensemble), <i>State Fair</i> (Abel Frake), The Pirates of Penzance (Samuel), <i>Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein's Cinderella</i> (King Maximillian), <i>Patience</i> (The Duke of Dunstable), <i>High Society</i> (Mike Connor), <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i> (Dick Deadeye), <i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i> (Bob Cratchit), <i>Naughty Marietta, Revised 2018</i> and <i>The Mikado</i> (Ensemble), and with other local theaters, <i>South Pacific</i> (Stewpot), <i>Seussical the Musical</i> (Horton), <i>The Wizard of OZ</i> (Uncle Henry). Jeff enjoys the shore, camping, Italian food, red wine, and hopes to revive his love of piano, and photography. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/statefair2025/headshots/Mark%20Teseny%20playbill.jpg" alt="Mark Teseny headshot" class="headshot" /></span><a name="Mark"></a><span class="person">Mark A. Teseny</span> (<span class="role">Set Designer</span>) has been involved in all aspects of theater production for 4 years. He first got involved in 2022 when his husband asked him if he would be interested in designing props for <i>Dial M For Murder</i>. Mark quickly fell in love with theater production and design, and has since worked at numerous theaters as Props Designer (<i>The Addams Family</i>, <i>'night Mother</i>, <i>Wizard of Oz</i>), Sound Designer (<i>Too Much Light Makes the Baby Go Blind</i>, <i>Peter Pan JR.</i>, <i>Frozen JR.</i>, <i>My Son Pinocchio JR.</i>), Sound Engineer (<i>Beauty &amp; the Beast</i>, <i>Legally Blonde</i>), Set Carpenter (<i>Legally Blonde</i>, <i>The Little Mermaid</i>, <i>Spongebob The Musical</i>), Master Carpenter (<i>Anastasia</i>), Scenic Designer (<i>Freaky Friday</i>, <i>How to Succeed in Bussiness Without Really Trying</i>), Stage Manager (<i>State Fair</i>, <i>Hello Dolly</i>), and Technical Director (<i>Pranksy</i>).  Mark would like to thank this amazing cast and crew for their collaboration, insight, and for being an amazing team to work with. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Lisette Walker a.jpg" alt="Lisette Walker headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Lisette"></a><span class="person">Lisette Walker</span> (<span class="role">Business Person</span>) has been performing on stage in the area since the Fall of 2012, after returning to the area following her husband's retirement from the US Navy.  By day, she works for the Department of Veterans Affairs as a Authorization Quality Review Specialist and is currently a Chief Petty Officer in the United States Navy Reserves. She sang in choir all through High School and College; and also sang with a Choir in Bosnia in 1999-2000. Her primary instrument is the Trumpet/Cornet which she played as a member of a Navy Band near Memphis, TN from 2000-2004 and played in band all through junior and senior high School and continued through college at West Chester University where she majored in music. In addition to performing with Ardensingers, she also plays with 2 bands: Penn View Brass Band and the Veterans Association of Military Musicians.  This is her first show with Rose Valley, and first Broadway style musical in over 30 years. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
          
               <p class="bios"><a name="SharonWC"></a><span class="headshot_img"><img src="https://archive.rvco.org/past_shows/patience2023/headshots/sharon.jpg" alt="Sharon Weil-Chalker headshot" class="headshot"/></span><span class="person">Sharon Weil-Chalker</span> (<span class="role">Charwomen, Secretary</span>) is thrilled to be back in her fifth RVCO production, including rehearsing <i>State Fair</i>, which wasn't staged due to the pandemic, followed by <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>, <i>Patience</i>, and <i>The Gondoliers</i>. She was so happy to end her prior several decades-long hiatus from theatre. Much gratitude to Florrie, Chris, and Caity for giving her this wonderful opportunity with this fun and talented cast. Sharon also sings baritone with Sweet Adelines/Philadelphia Freedom Chorus (women's barbershop). She previously sang with Northwestern University Singers, the Swarthmore College Chorus, and the Singing Moms. Tap was on her bucket list, so she has taken tap, salsa, and bachata lessons. Favourite roles: Sharon/By My Side (<i>Godspell</i>), Sylvia Barrett (<i>Up the Down Staircase</i>), and Handel's Messiah singalongs (and the never staged Hoopla Barker!). Off stage, Sharon is a physician who takes care of babies' hearts (way easier than singing and dancing at the same time), and enjoys hiking, gardening, going to the theatre, and dragon boating. She plays flute, some piano, and very (very) little guitar. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="headshots/Donna Winquist a.jpg" alt="Donna Winquist headshot" class="headshot lighter" /></span><a name="Donna"></a><span class="person">Donna Winquist</span> (<span class="role">Hedy LaRue, Board Member</span>) is excited, after 14 wonderful years of playing the French horn with RVCO, to see what it's like to perform onstage.  Donna's theatrical journey began (too many years ago) in several musical productions and an operetta. She now exercises her musical talents by performing in a number of community orchestras in the Philadelphia area and South Florida. She is thrilled beyond belief to be a part of this show and fully believes that it's never too late to do something you love. She thanks the cast and the larger RVCO family for their kindness and support. And she couldn't have done this without the additional support of her wonderful extended family, neighbors and friends.  Donna also deeply appreciates her three sons and their families for their encouragement and - with respect to the boys - for setting aside their embarrassment at having an onstage bimbo for a mom. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>
     
               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="../pirates2024/headshots/Sarah.jpg" alt="Sarah Norton headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Sarah"></a><span class="person">Sarah Norton</span> (<span class="role">Isabel</span>) is excited to return to RVCO as Isabel for her seventh G&amp;S show! She recently played Ruth in <i>Ruddigore</i> (2024) and Sacarissa (as well as being the understudy for Melissa) in <i>Princess Ida</i> (2023) with Ardensingers.  Sarah is proudly neurodivergent and disabled and is passionate about disability rights. She thanks her three rescue beagles for their continual support and goofy antics.  <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

               <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="../pirates2024/headshots/Brian.jpg" alt="Brian Rubino headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Brian"></a><span class="person">Brian Rubino</span> (<span class="role">Pirate Apprentice</span>) is thrilled to be one of the young recruits to this rollicking band of pirates! His RVCO credits include Very Young Scrooge in <i>A Christmas Carol - The Musical</i> (2019), Midshipmite in <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i> (2022), and Royal Page in <i>Rodger's and Hammerstein's Cinderella</i> (2024). Additional credits include playing Shrek in Upper Darby Summer Stage's 2024 Magic Makers showcase. Brian can also be found playing the cello and spell-casting in his middle school's D&amp;D club. <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>

                    <p class="bios"><span class="headshot_img"><img src="../pirates2024/headshots/Meagan.jpg" alt="Meagan Rubino headshot" class="headshot"/></span><a name="Meagan"></a><span class="person">Meagan Rubino</span> (<span class="role">Edith</span>) greets you gaily for another RVCO production! Previously with RVCO, she was obnoxious as Portia in <i>Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein's Cinderella</i>, aesthetic as Lady Ella in <i>Patience</i>, and served in Her Majesty's chorus on the <i>H.M.S. Pinafore</i>. She has also performed with the Penn Singers and the Philadelphia Gilbert &amp; Sullivan Union. Meagan is a proud member of the faculty of School of the Future in Philadelphia and an ardent advocate of public education and civil service in Upper Darby Township. To my McNuggets: &ldquo;I love you to the moon and back!&rdquo; To my own Pirate prince: &ldquo;That's some fine booty!&rdquo; <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>


                    <p class="bios"><a name="Fiona"></a><span class="headshot_img"><img src="../cinderella/headshots/Fiona.jpg" alt="Fiona Tillman headshot" class="headshot"/></span><span class="person">Fiona Tillman</span> (<span class="role">Pirate Apprentice</span>) is thrilled to be part of RVCO. She has been acting for 4 years in youth performances as well as participating in <i>Rodgers &amp; Hammerstein's Cinderella</i> in the spring. She has a love for both sports and music, and participates in softball and cross country as well as both chorus and band. She is so excited to be back for a second show with RVCO! <a href="#top" class="back2top">Back to top</a></p>



